{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["This prayer was spoken in the spirit of prophecy, and he prophesies concerning a famine that will come, as will become clear at the end of the prayer, and Israel will have no strength to stand against the enemy. This prayer follows the order of prayers, therefore he wrote <b>upon Shigionoth</b>, <b>to the chief musician</b>, and also the word <b>Selah</b>. I have explained these words in the book of Psalms."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:00.907865185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}